in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @facet/gestalt
in @facet/gleam

# @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam — the gestalt IR → gleam (via
# gestalt-ui library) value cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (gestalt IR) groups together at `shards/cascade/code/
# gestalt/`; target (gleam here) leafs at `shards/cascade/code/
# gestalt/gleam.mirror`.
#
# THIS species is the SECOND LEG of the composition theorem chain
# per Alex 2026-08-03 split-cascade directive (Q-C1):
#
#   *"Split cascade architecture: cascade<mirror, gestalt> +
#    cascade<gestalt, gleam> as separate species (not one combined
#    cascade). Opens door for cascade<gestalt, X> alternate
#    back-ends without touching mirror."*
#
# Per Alex 2026-08-03 Q-C2 verbatim:
#
#   *"cascade<gestalt, gleam> emits gestalt-ui-shaped Gleam (not
#    arbitrary Gleam)"*
#
# The emission target IS the existing gestalt-ui Gleam vocabulary
# crate at `/Users/reed/dev/projects/gestalt-ui/`. This cascade
# does NOT emit arbitrary Gleam — it emits Gleam that COMPOSES
# OVER the gestalt-ui library's Token/Theme/composite/view
# abstractions (per Taut scout §1.4 exported grammar).
#
# === Composition theorem chain (companion math 2026-08-03) ===
#
#   mirror substrate
#     ↓  @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt (sibling mint this arc)
#   gestalt IR (@facet/gestalt AST + .gestalt file surface)
#     ↓  @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam (THIS species)
#   gestalt-ui-shaped Gleam
#     ↓  @cascade/code/gleam/js (landed sibling per Taut scout §5)
#   JS bundle
#     → browser peer runtime @peer/browser (mint this arc)
#
# THIS cascade IS load-bearing for the composition-theorem chain
# closure. Without gestalt-ui-shaped emission, the chain cannot
# terminate at a browser peer runtime that consumes gestalt-ui
# tokens; arbitrary Gleam would require additional glue layer.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The gestalt-ui vocabulary crate ALREADY EXISTS at
# `/Users/reed/dev/projects/gestalt-ui/` (11 Gleam modules +
# tokens/*.dhall shadow-substrate + ui.conv mirror grammar per
# Taut scout 2026-08-03 §1). The composition target is not
# invented — it is Alex's existing target-agnostic vocabulary
# library that compiles to both BEAM and JS.
#
# This shard NAMES the cascade species that emits into that
# library; does not invent the library. Per [[feedback-substrate-
# already-had-the-word]] (~98th instance).
#
# === composition altitude: FILE-PROJECTION ↔ VOCABULARY-LIBRARY ===
#
# Source altitude: `@facet/gestalt` (shards/code/gestalt.mirror,
# this-arc landing) — .gestalt file-projection of the @gestalt
# graph.
#
# Target altitude: `@facet/gleam` (shards/code/gleam.mirror,
# 2026-06-06) — Gleam grammar; specifically the gestalt-ui subset
# per Q-C2 (Token(a) = Token(materialize: fn(Theme)->a,
# description) + composite.materialize_typography-shaped folds +
# view target-neutral view-models).
#
# Per companion spec §Composition theorem:
# - PRESERVED: register-honoring bytes (breath-marks + asymmetric
#   brackets + emoji + soft-breaks + corpus-links all lift to
#   Gleam string literals with source-position annotations); the
#   @document element structure (sections/paragraphs/spans map to
#   gestalt-ui view model constructors); the @user profile-optic
#   application (@user.project(theme) → gestalt-ui Theme record
#   modification).
# - LOST: mirror-substrate parametricity (labeled<v,m> collapses
#   to raw Gleam types); mirror-substrate bilateral verdict
#   states (cannot execute at Gleam runtime); mirror-substrate
#   family-root altitude discipline (Gleam has module-level
#   organization; not multi-altitude prism-family recursion).
#
# The `loss_lens<@facet/gestalt, @facet/gleam>` measures these gaps.
#
# === Gestalt-ui vocabulary composition constraints ===
#
# The emitted Gleam MUST compose over gestalt-ui's Token(a) type:
#
#   Token(materialize: fn(Theme) -> a, description: String)
#
# This is the LOAD-BEARING API constraint. Per gestalt-ui
# theme.gleam docblock (Alex 2026-02-28 verbatim): "Theme: the
# observation frame. Materialize collapses possibility space into
# actuality for a given theme."
#
# The cascade MUST emit tokens as Token(fn(Theme) -> concrete)
# instantiations, NOT as plain values. This ensures the browser
# peer runtime can theme-swap dynamically (light/dark; density
# compact/comfortable/spacious; motion full/reduced) WITHOUT
# re-invoking the cascade.
#
# Per Q-C2 gestalt-ui-shaped emit constraint (Alex 2026-08-03
# adjudication).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade family-root; Mara canonical
#   `ce4874b`, 2026-06-23): this species IS one of the cascade
#   species discharging the family-root.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor): gleam_
#   artifact uses labeled<> instance for gleam-value + gestalt-
#   ui-shape metadata.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from gestalt IR's file-projection basis
#   to gleam's module-value basis IS measurable via
#   `measure_gestalt_gleam`.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Elm-style Model/View/Update  Czaplicki 2012 Elm; ancestor of
#                                gestalt-ui's fn(Theme)->a
#                                materialize-as-collapse pattern.
#   Van Laarhoven 2007 lens      The Token(a) parametric wrapper
#                                composes over lens-style optics
#                                per @user's AffineTraversal/Lens/
#                                Traversal/Iso algebra.
#   Wadler 2003 + Bernardy 2017  doc-combinator algebra; render
#                                emits Gleam code via the same
#                                pretty-printer discipline both
#                                @facet/mirror.render and @facet/
#                                gestalt.render use.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-
#               canonical-spec.md §Composition theorem + §Cascade
#               leg spec §gestalt→gleam.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (Alex
#                      Q-C1 split-cascade + Q-C2 gestalt-ui-shaped
#                      emit directives),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (family-root),
#                 shards/labeled.mirror (functor primitive),
#                 shards/code/gestalt.mirror (source grammar; this-arc),
#                 shards/code/gleam.mirror (target grammar),
#                 shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror (sibling
#                                                             mint;
#                                                             first
#                                                             cascade
#                                                             leg),
#                 shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror (structural
#                                                            template
#                                                            precedent).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/gestalt/gleam.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/gestalt/gleam` per `@epistemologic/pact/
# path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-1989-theorems-for-free
source @arxiv/programming-languages/reynolds-1983-parametricity
source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-2003-prettier-printer
source @arxiv/programming-languages/bernardy-2017-pretty-not-greedy

prism @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === gestalt_source carrier ===
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=gestalt.
# References a gestalt IR (per @facet/gestalt) as unit of cascade.
type gestalt_source = ref

# === gestalt_ui_shape_metadata carrier ===
# Structured carrier for the gestalt-ui-shaped emit metadata per
# Q-C2 constraint:
#
#   token_bindings          — Token(a) instantiations for each
#                             .gestalt semantic-intent (per @ui/
#                             design color_intent + motion_intent +
#                             typography_intent enums).
#   theme_frame             — Theme record initialization per
#                             gestalt-ui theme.gleam Theme
#                             constructor.
#   composite_bindings      — Typography + Spacing + Surface
#                             composite constructor calls per
#                             gestalt-ui composite.gleam.
#   view_bindings           — SignalView / ActorView constructor
#                             calls per gestalt-ui view/*.gleam.
#   materialize_dispatch    — fn(Theme) -> a closure emissions
#                             per each token.
type gestalt_ui_shape_metadata = ref

# === gleam_artifact carrier ===
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4. A gleam_artifact
# IS a Gleam module ref annotated with gestalt_ui_shape_metadata.
type gleam_artifact = labeled(ref, gestalt_ui_shape_metadata)

# === apply_gestalt_gleam action ===
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the gestalt IR → gleam functor.
#
# Emission constraint per Q-C2: MUST emit Token(fn(Theme) -> a)
# instantiations, NOT plain values. Browser peer runtime theme-
# swaps dynamically without re-cascading.
#
# requires gestalt_source_well_formed(src, p): source parses per
# @facet/gestalt grammar discipline.
apply_gestalt_gleam(src: gestalt_source, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires gestalt_source_well_formed(src, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_gleam action ===
# Wraps a Gleam-module ref + gestalt-ui-shape metadata into a
# gleam_artifact via @labeled.label construction.
bundle_gleam(gleam_ref: ref, metadata: gestalt_ui_shape_metadata,
             p: perturbation) -> gleam_artifact
requires gestalt_ui_shape_coherent(gleam_ref, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_gestalt_gleam action ===
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the gestalt IR → gleam
# cascade.
measure_gestalt_gleam(src: gestalt_source, artifact: gleam_artifact,
                       p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(gleam_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires gestalt_gleam_loss_well_defined(src, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === Sub-bilaterals ===

bilateral gestalt_source_well_formed {
  sentinel "gestalt-source=parses-per-code-gestalt-grammar"
  arity 1
}
gestalt_source_well_formed(src: gestalt_source, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

bilateral gestalt_ui_shape_coherent {
  sentinel "gestalt-ui-shape=matches-vocabulary-library"
  arity 2
}
gestalt_ui_shape_coherent(gleam_ref: ref,
                            metadata: gestalt_ui_shape_metadata,
                            p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

bilateral gestalt_gleam_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
gestalt_gleam_loss_well_defined(src: gestalt_source,
                                  artifact: gleam_artifact,
                                  p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

bilateral cascade_gestalt_gleam_admissible {
  sentinel "cascade=gestalt-ui-vocabulary-shaped"
  arity 1
}
cascade_gestalt_gleam_admissible(cascade_outcome: gleam_artifact)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === Composed bilateral ===
bilateral gestalt_gleam_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
gestalt_gleam_cascade_well_formed(src: gestalt_source,
                                    artifact: gleam_artifact,
                                    p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires gestalt_source_well_formed(src, p)
requires gestalt_ui_shape_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires gestalt_gleam_loss_well_defined(src, artifact, p)
requires cascade_gestalt_gleam_admissible(artifact)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam
out gestalt_source
out gestalt_ui_shape_metadata
out gleam_artifact
out apply_gestalt_gleam
out bundle_gleam
out measure_gestalt_gleam
out gestalt_source_well_formed
out gestalt_ui_shape_coherent
out gestalt_gleam_loss_well_defined
out cascade_gestalt_gleam_admissible
out gestalt_gleam_cascade_well_formed
